   "pearl": "trans introduction",
   "map": "Trans_Introduction",
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "one matrix does it all. move, turn, grow — the same multiplication. what stays the same is the invariant. homogeneous coordinates: a point and a direction differ by one number.",
     "by": "claude"
    },
    {
     "token": "homogeneous_coordinates",
     "text": "a point carries a 1, a direction carries a 0 — that is the whole difference",
     "by": "claude"
    },
    {
     "token": "invariants_demo",
     "text": "what does not change when everything moves",
     "by": "claude"
    },
    {
     "token": "rotation_gimbal",
     "text": "three rings, and one way to lose a degree of freedom",
     "by": "claude"
    },
    {
     "token": "matrix_4x4_viewer",
     "text": "sixteen numbers. every move you will ever make",
     "by": "claude"
    },
    {
     "token": "transform_composition",
     "text": "one after another is one. order matters",
     "by": "claude"
    },
    {
     "token": "balance_puzzle",
     "text": "the transform you cannot see: weight",
     "by": "claude"
    }
